<p>I recently got to read an advance copy of Geoffrey Cain’s new book, “<a href="https://geoffreycain.net/steve-jobs-in-exile/">Steve Jobs In Exile</a>: The Untold Story of NeXT and the Remaking of an American Visionary,” which was published this week. It’s a surprising and sometimes gruesome (in a businessy way) story that does not show off the famous man at the center of the story as much as depict all the ways he failed in what turned out to be preparation for his career-defining role as Apple CEO. (I also got to <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bUjTxiddazc&amp;t=2862s">interview Cain about the book</a> this week on Upgrade.)</p>
